1. Definitions

"Software" means everything in this repository and in its history: source code, kernels, scripts, documentation, the
paper, figures, measurements, and every binary built from any of them.

"Licensor" means Shaban Ejupi.

"You" means the natural person who obtains the Software. A company, partnership, foundation, association, public body,
government, army or any other organization is never "You" under section 2, and neither is a person acting for one.

"Output" means anything produced by running the Software or anything derived from it: trained adapters, model weights,
checkpoints, gradients, digests, logs, benchmark numbers and any model or dataset made with their help.

"Personal Study" means reading the Software and running it privately, on hardware You own, to learn how it works.

"Academic Research" means non-commercial research by a person enrolled at or employed by an accredited university, not
funded, directed or owned by a company, a government body or an army, whose results are published openly and in full.

"Commercial Use" means every use that is not Personal Study or Academic Research, including: any use by or for an
organization; use in or for a product, service, consultancy, hosted or cloud offering; training, tuning or evaluating
models that are used, offered or shared beyond Personal Study or Academic Research; and any use that brings You or anyone
else money, savings or any other advantage, directly or indirectly.

2. The free permissions -- the only ones

While You comply with every section of this license, and for no other purpose, You may:
  (a) read the Software;
  (b) for Personal Study: build it and run it on hardware You own, privately, for at most 90 days in total counted from
      the first time You run any part of it;
  (c) for Academic Research: build it and run it on hardware You own or that Your university provides, for the duration
      of the research project, and publish the scientific results with the attribution of section 5.
Nothing else is permitted. Rights not expressly granted are reserved.

